@cover Welcome to Jotstak
  Five minutes, six steps

This is a Jotstak document. Change anything in it and watch the page follow.
@note This copy is yours to break.

## 1. It is Markdown

Everything you know from Markdown already works: **bold**, *italic*, `code`, [links](https://jotstak.pages.dev) and lists.

- Press Enter and the line breaks.
- Leave a blank line and a new paragraph starts.

==Try it:== add a third point to the list above.

## 2. A note in the margin

A line starting with `@note` goes in the margin, beside the line before it.
@note Like this one.

==Try it:== add a note of your own under this line.

## 3. Blocks

A line that starts with `@` is a block. Its settings go on that line; what goes inside it is indented underneath.

@decision title="Write our specs in Jotstak" status=proposed
  context: Our PRDs are spread across five tools
  choice: One plain-text file per spec
  consequences: Diagrams sit beside the words that explain them

==Try it:== change `status=proposed` to `status=accepted`.

## 4. Diagrams from indentation

Indent a line under another and it becomes its child. That is all a diagram needs.

@tree dir=down nodes=boxed
  Launch
    Docs
    Extension
    Playground

==Try it:== add a fourth line under Launch, indented like the others.

## 5. Every block, one keystroke away

Type `@` at the start of a line in VS Code, or click a tile in the playground: every block, ready to fill in.

## 6. Hand it on

What you see is what prints, page for page: download a PDF or a Word file from the playground, or use **Jotstak: Export…** in VS Code. Every block is explained at [jotstak.pages.dev/docs](https://jotstak.pages.dev/docs/).
